    <section class="section" id="environment">
      <div class="section-header"><h3>Environment variables</h3></div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Required</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>S3_ENDPOINT</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>MinIO API base URL, e.g. <code><%= endpoint %></code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>S3_REGION</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Region string, e.g. <code><%= region %></code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>S3_BUCKET</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Your bucket name from the storage page</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>S3_ACCESS_KEY</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Access key from an app key integration</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>S3_SECRET_KEY</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>Secret key shown once when the key was created</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="muted small">Add <code>.env</code> to <code>.gitignore</code> before your first commit — a leaked secret key gives full access to that bucket until you remove the key on the storage page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================================================== -->
    <section class="section" id="limits">
      <div class="section-header"><h3>Rules and limits</h3></div>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><strong>One bucket per key:</strong> an app key is scoped to the bucket it was created from. Using it on another bucket returns <code>AccessDenied</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Ownership is enforced twice:</strong> the portal only lists/operates your own buckets, and MinIO policies block anyone else's keys from touching them.</li>
          <li><strong>No upload size limit</strong> on the portal; your own app can stream any size with the SDK (use disk storage or multipart uploads for very large files).</li>
          <li><strong>Bucket names</strong> must be 1–24 characters, lowercase letters/numbers/hyphens, and are automatically prefixed with your username. The default <code>&lt;username&gt;-workspace</code> bucket cannot be deleted.</li>
          <li><strong>Buckets must be empty</strong> before deletion — delete the objects first.</li>
          <li><strong>Secrets are shown once.</strong> There is no “view password” — create a new key if lost.</li>
          <li><strong>Backend only:</strong> never embed access/secret keys in browser JavaScript, mobile apps, or public repos.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================================================== -->
    <section class="section" id="troubleshooting">
      <div class="section-header"><h3>Troubleshooting connection errors</h3></div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Error</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>AccessDenied</code></td>
                <td>Key scoped to a different bucket, or the key was removed</td>
                <td>Use the bucket the key was created for, or create a fresh app key on the storage page</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>InvalidAccessKeyId</code></td>
                <td>Access key typo or deleted key</td>
                <td>Re-copy the access key; recreate the integration if it was removed</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>SignatureDoesNotMatch</code></td>
                <td>Wrong secret key</td>
                <td>Re-enter the secret exactly as shown at creation (no quotes/spaces in .env)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>NoSuchBucket</code></td>
                <td>Bucket name mismatch</td>
                <td>Copy the exact bucket name from the storage page — names include your username prefix</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>ECONNREFUSED</code> / fetch failed / timeout</td>
                <td>Wrong endpoint host/port, or MinIO is down</td>
                <td>Check <code>S3_ENDPOINT</code> includes the scheme and port; retry the Test Connection button on the storage page</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Request goes to <code>bucket.host</code> and fails DNS</td>
                <td>Missing <code>forcePathStyle: true</code></td>
                <td>Add <code>forcePathStyle: true</code> to the S3Client options</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>MulterError: Unexpected field</code></td>
                <td>Form field name is not <code>file</code></td>
                <td>Name the form field <code>file</code> or change <code>upload.single("file")</code> to match</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>403 with empty body on download</td>
                <td>Object key doesn't exist or belongs to another bucket</td>
                <td>List the bucket first and use the exact <code>Key</code> returned</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="muted small">Still stuck? Open the Storage workspace and press <em>Test Connection</em>-style verification: if the portal lists your bucket and files, the storage service is healthy and the problem is in your app's five connection details.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

